{"code":"49-9051.00","title":"Electrical Power-Line Installers and Repairers","description":"Install or repair cables or wires used in electrical power or distribution systems. May erect poles and light or heavy duty transmission towers.","jobZone":2,"kinds":{"R":{"score":7,"share":0.5208},"I":{"score":2.66,"share":0.1441},"A":{"score":1,"share":0},"S":{"score":1.28,"share":0.0243},"E":{"score":1.78,"share":0.0677},"C":{"score":3.8,"share":0.2431}},"highPoints":["R","C"],"tasks":[{"id":8412,"text":"Adhere to safety practices and procedures, such as checking equipment regularly and erecting barriers around work areas.","core":true,"importance":4.77,"relevance":100,"frequency":6.03},{"id":8418,"text":"Drive vehicles equipped with tools and materials to job sites.","core":true,"importance":4.75,"relevance":100,"frequency":6.09},{"id":8413,"text":"Open switches or attach grounding devices to remove electrical hazards from disturbed or fallen lines or to facilitate repairs.","core":true,"importance":4.7,"relevance":100,"frequency":4.61},{"id":8414,"text":"Climb poles or use truck-mounted buckets to access equipment.","core":true,"importance":4.55,"relevance":99.73,"frequency":5.68},{"id":8416,"text":"Install, maintain, and repair electrical distribution and transmission systems, including conduits, cables, wires, and related equipment, such as transformers, circuit breakers, and switches.","core":true,"importance":4.51,"relevance":100,"frequency":5.07},{"id":8420,"text":"Inspect and test power lines and auxiliary equipment to locate and identify problems, using reading and testing instruments.","core":true,"importance":4.5,"relevance":97.83,"frequency":5.02},{"id":8419,"text":"Coordinate work assignment preparation and completion with other workers.","core":true,"importance":4.46,"relevance":100,"frequency":5.36},{"id":8423,"text":"Replace or straighten damaged poles.","core":true,"importance":4.44,"relevance":100,"frequency":4.19},{"id":8421,"text":"String wire conductors and cables between poles, towers, trenches, pylons, and buildings, setting lines in place and using winches to adjust tension.","core":true,"importance":4.43,"relevance":99.73,"frequency":4.47},{"id":8425,"text":"Attach cross-arms, insulators, and auxiliary equipment to poles prior to installing them.","core":true,"importance":4.37,"relevance":99.24,"frequency":4.72},{"id":8427,"text":"Dig holes, using augers, and set poles, using cranes and power equipment.","core":true,"importance":4.35,"relevance":99.73,"frequency":5},{"id":8426,"text":"Travel in trucks, helicopters, and airplanes to inspect lines for freedom from obstruction and adequacy of insulation.","core":true,"importance":4.29,"relevance":97.24,"frequency":4.42},{"id":8417,"text":"Identify defective sectionalizing devices, circuit breakers, fuses, voltage regulators, transformers, switches, relays, or wiring, using wiring diagrams and electrical-testing instruments.","core":true,"importance":4.23,"relevance":97.83,"frequency":3.82},{"id":8424,"text":"Install watt-hour meters and connect service drops between power lines and consumers' facilities.","core":true,"importance":4.2,"relevance":100,"frequency":4.12},{"id":8422,"text":"Test conductors, according to electrical diagrams and specifications, to identify corresponding conductors and to prevent incorrect connections.","core":true,"importance":4.14,"relevance":86.9,"frequency":3.69},{"id":8415,"text":"Place insulating or fireproofing materials over conductors and joints.","core":true,"importance":4.02,"relevance":86.41,"frequency":4.3},{"id":8429,"text":"Splice or solder cables together or to overhead transmission lines, customer service lines, or street light lines, using hand tools, epoxies, or specialized equipment.","core":true,"importance":4.02,"relevance":97.36,"frequency":4.26},{"id":8428,"text":"Trim trees that could be hazardous to the functioning of cables or wires.","core":true,"importance":3.85,"relevance":100,"frequency":3.38},{"id":8431,"text":"Clean, tin, and splice corresponding conductors by twisting ends together or by joining ends with metal clamps and soldering connections.","core":false,"importance":3.77,"relevance":60.84,"frequency":4},{"id":8432,"text":"Pull up cable by hand from large reels mounted on trucks.","core":true,"importance":3.75,"relevance":99.73,"frequency":3.77},{"id":8433,"text":"Lay underground cable directly in trenches, or string it through conduit running through the trenches.","core":true,"importance":3.36,"relevance":80.86,"frequency":3.07},{"id":8434,"text":"Cut trenches for laying underground cables, using trenchers and cable plows.","core":true,"importance":3.29,"relevance":77.81,"frequency":2.89},{"id":8430,"text":"Cut and peel lead sheathing and insulation from defective or newly installed cables and conduits prior to splicing.","core":true,"importance":3.16,"relevance":72.22,"frequency":3.16}],"activities":[{"id":"4.A.3.a.4","importance":4.67},{"id":"4.A.3.a.1","importance":4.6},{"id":"4.A.3.a.2","importance":4.41},{"id":"4.A.1.b.2","importance":4.38},{"id":"4.A.3.a.3","importance":4.37},{"id":"4.A.1.a.1","importance":4.3},{"id":"4.A.2.b.1","importance":4.29},{"id":"4.A.1.b.1","importance":4.09},{"id":"4.A.1.a.2","importance":3.83},{"id":"4.A.4.a.2","importance":3.73},{"id":"4.A.4.b.3","importance":3.44},{"id":"4.A.2.a.3","importance":3.31},{"id":"4.A.4.b.5","importance":3.25},{"id":"4.A.2.b.6","importance":3.2},{"id":"4.A.3.b.4","importance":3.18},{"id":"4.A.2.a.2","importance":3.13},{"id":"4.A.2.b.4","importance":3.13},{"id":"4.A.4.a.4","importance":3.13},{"id":"4.A.4.b.1","importance":3.08},{"id":"4.A.1.b.3","importance":3.07},{"id":"4.A.4.b.4","importance":3.05},{"id":"4.A.2.b.3","importance":3.02},{"id":"4.A.4.a.8","importance":3},{"id":"4.A.3.b.5","importance":2.98},{"id":"4.A.4.a.1","importance":2.98},{"id":"4.A.2.a.1","importance":2.96},{"id":"4.A.4.a.3","importance":2.93},{"id":"4.A.2.b.2","importance":2.82},{"id":"4.A.4.a.5","importance":2.81},{"id":"4.